clean_summary:
Really clean approach. Do cross entropy loss on the environment feedback. This allows the model to get supervision even on failed rollouts and helps form a sort of pseudo world model.

In reinforcement learning, a rollout is a trajectory of the agent acting in its environment; usually only successful rollouts that reach the reward provide a clear learning signal, so getting supervision from failed ones too is a way to use data that would otherwise be wasted.

